Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
"1","PCIE","Testable: writeAsRead; Value After Reset: 0x0","pcie0_dbi_dsp_reg_wr_rd_test","Validate PCIe DBI/PL register blocks by checking default reset values and verifying masked write/read integrity across the DBI, AER, MSI, iATU, and Link Control register set. Certain status/next-pointer and debug registers are excluded from default checks. The test writes multiple data patterns to writable fields, reads back, and compares against expected values considering read/write masks and preserved reset bits.","The test iterates over CNT=775 DBI/PL register addresses (addr_array). Phase 1: Default check (chk_rst_val) skips any address with read_mask=0 and also skips three specific addresses (mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF). For each remaining address, it reads data_rd=read_reg(addr) and compares with default_value_array[i]; increments def_fail_cnt on mismatch. Phase 2: Write/Read check (chk_rd_wr) runs for six data patterns: 0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0x00000000, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000. For each pattern, it writes only to addresses not flagged in skip_array and with write_mask!=0. It then reads back only from addresses with read_mask!=0 and write_mask!=0. Expected value is exp_val = (data_wr & read_mask & write_mask) | ((~write_mask) & read_mask & default_value). If data_rd!=exp_val, wr_fail_cnt++. Final finish(0) if both counters are zero, else finish(1).","NA","Polling","NA","NA","Non-readable registers are skipped based on read masks; non-writable registers are skipped based on write masks; additional addresses are excluded via a skip list. Default-value checks exclude DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, and DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF. Reads after writes are expected to reflect only writable, readable fields while preserving reset values for non-writable bits.","1) Initialize the test and load the PCIe DBI/PL address and mask tables. 2) Default reset validation: For each readable register, read and compare against its expected reset value; skip DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, and DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF. 3) Write/read integrity: For each of six data patterns, write the pattern to all registers that are not skipped and are writable, then read back only the readable and writable registers. 4) Compare each readback to the masked expectation, preserving reset values for non-writable fields. 5) Aggregate results and declare PASS only if no mismatches are observed.","1) chk_rst_val(): for i in 0..CNT-1: addr=addr_array[i]; if read_mask_array[i]==0 continue; if addr in {mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF} continue; data_rd=read_reg(addr); if data_rd==default_value_array[i] pass else def_fail_cnt++. 2) chk_rd_wr(): patterns={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0x00000000,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}; for each data_wr: (a) write phase: for each i: if skip_array[i]==1 continue; if write_mask_array[i]==0 continue; write_reg(addr_array[i], data_wr). (b) read/compare: for each i: if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0 or read_mask_array[i]==0 continue; data_rd=read_reg(addr); wr_n=(write_mask_array[i]^0xffffffff); exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); if data_rd!=exp_val wr_fail_cnt++. 3) if (def_fail_cnt>0 || wr_fail_cnt>0) finish(1) else finish(0).","DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF, DBI_DSP_MSI_CTRL_INT_0_EN_OFF, DBI_DSP_IATU_REGION_CTRL_1_OFF_OUTBOUND_0, DBI_DSP_LINK_CONTROL_LINK_STATUS_REG, DBI_DSP_AER_EXT_CAP_HDR_OFF, DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL2_DEVICE_STATUS2_REG","mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_MSI_CTRL_INT_0_EN_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_IATU_REGION_CTRL_1_OFF_OUTBOUND_0, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_LINK_CONTROL_LINK_STATUS_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_AER_EXT_CAP_HDR_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL2_DEVICE_STATUS2_REG","PASS if: (a) all readable registers match their reset values (excluding the specified status/next-pointer and debug registers), and (b) for each data pattern, all readable+writable registers read back values that match the masked expectation with non-writable bits preserved at reset values. FAIL otherwise.","Require data_rd == default_value_array[i] for all eligible i in default check. For write/read, for all eligible i and each data pattern: data_rd == ((data_wr & read_mask & write_mask) | ((~write_mask) & read_mask & default_value)). Final finish(0) iff def_fail_cnt==0 && wr_fail_cnt==0; else finish(1).","Not","#include <stdio.h>, #include <stdlib.h>, #include \"test_common.h\", #include \"test_define.c\", #include <pcie.h>","#define CNT 775, #define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000, #define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000","NA"
"2","PCIE","Testable: writeAsRead; Value After Reset: 0x0","pcie0_dbi_usp_reg_wr_rd_test","Validate PCIe DBI/PL register blocks (USP) by checking default reset values and verifying masked write/read behavior across DBI, AER, MSI, iATU, and Link Control registers. Certain status/next-pointer and debug registers are excluded from default checks. Multiple data patterns are written to writable fields and compared against expected values considering masks and preserved reset bits.","Iterates CNT=775 addresses from addr_array. Default check: skip read_mask==0 and also skip mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF; reads data and compares with default_value_array; increments def_fail_cnt on mismatch. Write/Read check: for patterns {0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0x00000000,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}, writes data_wr to addresses not in skip_array and with write_mask!=0; reads back only where read_mask!=0 and write_mask!=0; expected exp_val computed using read/write masks with non-writable bits preserved from defaults; increments wr_fail_cnt on mismatch. Final finish based on counters.","NA","Polling","NA","NA","Default reset checks exclude DBI_USP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, DBI_USP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, and DBI_USP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF. Non-readable and non-writable registers are skipped per masks; additional exclusions are applied via a skip list. Readbacks must reflect writable fields only; non-writable bits remain at reset values.","1) Load the DBI/PL USP register address and mask tables. 2) Validate default reset values for all readable registers, excluding DBI_USP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, DBI_USP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, and DBI_USP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF. 3) For six data patterns, write all writable, non-skipped registers and then read back only the readable+writable ones. 4) For each readback, compare against masked expectations preserving reset-only fields. 5) Report PASS if no mismatches are found across all data patterns.","1) chk_rst_val(): for i=0..CNT-1: if read_mask_array[i]==0 continue; if addr in {mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF} continue; data_rd=read_reg(addr); compare to default_value_array[i]; if mismatch def_fail_cnt++. 2) chk_rd_wr(): for each data_wr in {0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0x00000000,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}: (a) writes: if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask==0 skip; else write_reg(addr,data_wr). (b) reads: if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask==0 or read_mask==0 skip; else data_rd=read_reg(addr); exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask & write_mask) | ((~write_mask) & read_mask & default_value)); if data_rd!=exp_val wr_fail_cnt++. 3) finish(0) if both counters zero else finish(1).","DBI_USP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, DBI_USP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, DBI_USP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF, DBI_USP_MSI_CTRL_INT_0_EN_OFF, DBI_USP_IATU_REGION_CTRL_1_OFF_OUTBOUND_0, DBI_USP_LINK_CONTROL_LINK_STATUS_REG","mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_MSI_CTRL_INT_0_EN_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_IATU_REGION_CTRL_1_OFF_OUTBOUND_0, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_USP_LINK_CONTROL_LINK_STATUS_REG","PASS if all readable registers match reset values (excluding listed exceptions) and all readable+writable registers match masked expectations across all data patterns. FAIL otherwise.","Require data_rd == default_value_array[i] for default checks. For each eligible i and each pattern, require data_rd == ((data_wr & read_mask & write_mask) | ((~write_mask) & read_mask & default_value)). Final finish(0) iff def_fail_cnt==0 && wr_fail_cnt==0; else finish(1).","Not","#include <stdio.h>, #include <stdlib.h>, #include \"test_common.h\", #include \"test_define.c\", #include <pcie.h>","#define CNT 775, #define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000, #define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000","NA"
"3","PCIE","Testable: writeAsRead; Value After Reset: 0x0","pcie0_sii_rc_reg_wr_rd_test","Validate the PCIe SII RC register block by checking default reset values and verifying masked write/read integrity across SII configuration, control, MSI, and diagnostic registers. The PHY reset control register is excluded from default-value checks. The test writes multiple data patterns to writable fields and verifies readbacks with masks preserving reset-only bits.","Iterates CNT=153 SII RC addresses. Default check (chk_rst_val): skip any non-readable address and also skip mizar_PCIE0_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL; read and compare against default_value_array; increment def_fail_cnt on mismatch. Write/Read (chk_rd_wr): for patterns {0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0x00000000,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}, write to addresses not in skip_array and with write_mask!=0; read back only when read_mask!=0 and write_mask!=0; compute expected value with masks and preserved default bits; increment wr_fail_cnt on mismatch. Final status via finish(0/1).","NA","Polling","NA","NA","Default-value checks exclude SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL. Non-readable and non-writable registers are skipped per masks; additional exclusions applied via skip list. Readbacks are validated against masked expectations; reset-only bits remain unchanged.","1) Load SII RC register address and mask tables. 2) Validate default reset values for each readable register, excluding SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL. 3) For six data patterns, write to all writable, non-skipped registers and read back only those that are readable and writable. 4) Compare each readback using read/write masks and preserved reset values. 5) Pass only if no mismatches occur.","1) chk_rst_val(): for i=0..CNT-1: if read_mask==0 continue; if addr==mizar_PCIE0_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL continue; data_rd=read_reg(addr); if data_rd!=default_value_array[i] def_fail_cnt++. 2) chk_rd_wr(): for each data_wr in {0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0x00000000,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}: (a) writes: if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask==0 skip; else write_reg(addr,data_wr). (b) reads: if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask==0 or read_mask==0 skip; else data_rd=read_reg(addr); exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask & write_mask) | ((~write_mask) & read_mask & default_value)); if data_rd!=exp_val wr_fail_cnt++. 3) Finalize with finish(0/1).","SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL","mizar_PCIE0_SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL","PASS if all readable registers (excluding SII_PHY_RST_CONTROL) match reset values and all readable+writable registers match masked expectations across all data patterns. FAIL otherwise.","Default check requires data_rd == default_value_array[i] for eligible i. Write/read requires data_rd == ((data_wr & read_mask & write_mask) | ((~write_mask) & read_mask & default_value)) for eligible i across all patterns. Final finish(0) iff def_fail_cnt==0 && wr_fail_cnt==0; else finish(1).","Not","#include <stdio.h>, #include <stdlib.h>, #include \"test_common.h\", #include \"test_define.c\", #include <pcie0/pcie_sii_rc_def.h>, #include <pcie0/pcie_sii_rc_offset.h>","#define MIZAR_PCIE0_SII_BASE 0xE68C0000, #define CNT 153, #define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000, #define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000","NA"
"4","PCIE","Per-Function PCIe Capabilities and BAR Config; Per-Function PCIe Capabilities and BAR Config / Physical Function 0 (PF0) / PCI Express Capability","pcie_cfg_wr_rd_test","Program coherency control fields in the PCIe DBI for multiple instances, poll SII status until the link is ready, then perform PCIe configuration space BAR programming and command register enables. Use a handshake register to synchronize completion. Validate by successful polling exit and final synchronization.","The test optionally triggers link training (via compile-time selects). It programs DBI coherency fields by setting specific bitfields in DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF for PCIe0 and PCIe1. It then polls the SII0 status register at offset 0xC0 until masked bits equal 0xD1, and if DM1_RC is enabled, similarly polls SII1. After writing 0x11111111 to address 0xE6004100 and a delay, it performs configuration space operations: for DM0_RC, calls mem_base_program_dm0_x4(), reads initial header registers, writes 0xFFFFFFFF to BAR-related offsets (0x10..0x24), reads them back, then writes BAR values (0x0,0x4,0x20000000,0x40000000,0x60000000,0x80000000) and enables Memory/IO/Bus Master by writing 0x7 to offset 0x4. For DM1_RC, similar sequence using the second instance accessors. Finally, it waits until read_reg(0xE6004100)==0x12345678, then calls finish(0).","NA","Polling","NA","NA","Requires link training sequences per compile-time selection and readiness indication via SII status polling. Coherency fields are adjusted in DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF. External environment must drive the handshake register at 0xE6004100 to 0x12345678 to complete the test.","1) Initialize and, if enabled, perform link training for the selected PCIe instances. 2) Configure coherency settings by updating fields in DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF for each PCIe instance. 3) Poll SII status to confirm link readiness before proceeding. 4) For each enabled Root Complex instance, program memory base and read initial configuration space headers. 5) Perform BAR sizing writes and reads, then program BAR base addresses and enable Memory/IO/Bus Master in the Command register. 6) Wait for the external completion handshake to assert on 0xE6004100, then declare PASS.","1) write_reg(0xE6004100,0x0); optional link_training_* calls under DMx_* macros. 2) For each of PCIe0 and PCIe1: rd_wr_data1=read_reg(mizar_PCIE{0,1}_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF); rd_wr_data1=set_data for bitfield ranges; write_reg back. 3) Poll: while ((read_sii0_reg(0xC0) & 0xD1) != 0xD1) continue; if DM1_RC enabled, similarly poll read_sii1_reg(0xC0). 4) write_reg(0xE6004100,0x11111111); wait_on(15000). 5) If DM0_RC: mem_base_program_dm0_x4(); read_pcie_slv0_reg in a loop; write_pcie_slv0_reg 0xFFFFFFFF to offsets 0x10..0x24; read back; then write BAR values {0x0,0x4,0x20000000,0x40000000,0x60000000,0x80000000}; set Command (offset 0x4) to 0x7. 6) If DM1_RC: analogous sequence using *slv1* functions. 7) Poll read_reg(0xE6004100) until 0x12345678; finish(0).","DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF","mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF, mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF","PASS if SII status polling completes (indicating link ready) and the final handshake register at 0xE6004100 transitions to 0x12345678, resulting in finish(0).","Require loop exit when (read_sii0_reg(0xC0) & 0xD1) == 0xD1 (and similarly for SII1 if enabled). Require final loop exit when read_reg(0xE6004100) == 0x12345678; then finish(0).","Not","#include <stdlib.h>, #include <stdio.h>, #include <test_common.h>, #include \"pcie.h\"","NA","NA"